<Site
  title="Just Sign It — Sign a PDF in your browser"
  description="Sign PDFs right in your browser. Nothing gets uploaded, so your file never leaves your computer. Free, no account."
>
  <h1>Sign PDFs <mark>right in your browser.</mark></h1>
  <p>Open a PDF, add your signature, and download the signed copy. Nothing gets uploaded, so your file <mark>never leaves your computer.</mark></p>
  <p>It’s free and you don’t need an account.</p>
  <p class="cta"><a href="/sign" class="btn primary">Sign a PDF</a></p>

  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Opens any PDF. Drop it on the page or pick it from your files.</li>
    <li>Lets you draw your signature, type your name in a handwriting font, or upload a photo of it. If you upload a photo, it can remove the white background.</li>
    <li>Saves more than one signature, so you can keep your full signature and your initials.</li>
    <li>Puts a signature anywhere on any page. Drag to move it, use the corner to resize it, and use the arrow keys to nudge it.</li>
    <li>Downloads a new PDF with your signatures on it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why it works this way</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your file stays on your computer.</strong> Leases, contracts and tax forms are private. There’s no server here to send them to.</li>
    <li><strong>No account.</strong> You shouldn’t need to sign up just to sign one page.</li>
    <li><strong>It only remembers your signatures if you ask it to.</strong> Check “Remember my signatures” to save them on your device. Leave it off on shared computers.</li>
    <li><strong>It’s an image of your signature.</strong> It isn’t a certified digital signature.</li>
  </ul>
</Site>
